## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Combat
## Notes: Sane UI's frames for the fight, being built. Your frame, your target's and your focus's in a nameplate's look, their targets and your pet under them, your cast and breath part of your frame; one frame for your party and raid, up to forty, sized in Edit Mode; your marks of auras and their icons where you track them; rings around the mouse for your global cooldown and cast; a threat and damage meter of your group; frames out of sight at rest.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\SaneUI_Combat\Art\icon
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its words and settings. First: the other files will add to that table.
Combat.lua
# The nameplates' words and switches, added to Combat's; their start and their giving back (Nameplates/)
Nameplates\Nameplates.lua
# The module's switches handed to Core, every part's now in the list
Settings.lua
# The nameplates: the game's plates in our dress (the addon SaneUI_Nameplates until 2026-11-18)
# The health bar: round at both ends, its border by rank, a ring on your target and focus, the power line, the glow
Nameplates\Bar.lua
# The line inside the bar: quest, raid marker, level, item level, threat, name, health; the bar as wide as the line
Nameplates\Text.lua
# Your debuffs above the bar, a foe's buffs left of it, crowd control right of it, in the game's own aura containers
Nameplates\Auras.lua
# The raid marker, in the line
Nameplates\Marks.lua
# Your combo points on the power line of your target's bar
Nameplates\Resource.lua
# Plates smaller far away: their own size at your feet, half at 40 yards, a quarter at 60
Nameplates\Scale.lua
# Your target out of reach of all your attacks: its border red
Nameplates\Range.lua
# A unit's cast, under its plate's bar: icon with the seconds left, the spell and its target
Nameplates\Cast.lua
# The combat text: what a unit takes rising over its plate, and over your character; drawings for misses, parries, blocks
Nameplates\CombatText.lua
# Our dress on each plate the game shows, laid over its health bar; the game's own bar, name, auras and marks out of sight under it
Nameplates\Plate.lua
# A made-up plate drawn by the plates' own code, for the setup: what the settings change shows on it at once
Nameplates\Sample.lua
# The setup, step by step: each step's words, the switches it is about and its sample plates (the window is the addon Onboarding's)
Nameplates\Setup.lua
# A mark beside a creature's nameplate while it belongs to an objective of your quests still to do
QuestMarks.lua
# Rings around the mouse for the global cooldown and your cast, only while they run
MouseRings.lua
# Unit frames: ours for you, your target and your focus, in a nameplate's look, in place of the game's (Units/)
# The bar: round and green, its border, the rank's line, the glow, the power line; the row under it
Units\Bar.lua
# The line inside it: level and raid marker left, then the name, the health right; the row's name
Units\Text.lua
# The auras that matter most around them, in the game's own aura containers; the right click on an icon
Units\Auras.lua
# Those auras out of a fight, on icons of ours the mouse can reach: your tooltip, the menu, a frame at rest shown
Units\AuraRow.lua
# Your marks of auras: Important, Unimportant, Hidden, and their window (/sane auras)
Units\Lists.lua
# The game's list of your buffs and debuffs with those marks on it; the right click on it
Units\BuffList.lua
# Your cast as part of your frame, in place of the game's cast bar
Units\Cast.lua
# Your breath and the game's other timers on you as part of your frame, in place of its bars
Units\Timers.lua
# The frames and their rows (their targets, your pet): the game's secure unit buttons, placed in Edit Mode
Units\Units.lua
# Look out for, in your focus's place while you have none: a name or one of your group, focused by a click
Units\LookOut.lua
# Your party and raid: one member's frame, the tools behind your own slot, and the one window for them all
Units\GroupFace.lua
Units\GroupTools.lua
Units\Group.lua
# Reminders of buffs and debuffs: what shows when, those on the party and raid frames and on the nameplates, the
# invisible bars, the window
Reminders\Reminders.lua
Reminders\Group.lua
Reminders\Plates.lua
Reminders\Bars.lua
Reminders\Editor.lua
# The game's red error text off, by a switch
ErrorText.lua
# The threat and damage meter: threat added up, what the game tells of a fight, which bars a character has, the fights and
# saved ones, one character's row, the buttons on the first line, the window
Meter\Threat.lua
Meter\Read.lua
Meter\Shows.lua
Meter\Fights.lua
Meter\Row.lua
Meter\Controls.lua
Meter\Meter.lua
# Combat's setup, step by step: the parts, the unit frames, the party and raid frames with their preview and
# Edit Mode, the nameplates' steps, aura tracking (the window is the addon Onboarding's). Last: it draws every part
Setup.lua
